{"type":"text","timestamp":1788216054245,"sessionID":"ses_fa606ac90ffe98xXrlhK72YTFi","part":{"id":"prt_059fb7ac9001G3IlacTA68bPPl","messageID":"msg_059fb7365001Ti3s125lpH68HL","sessionID":"ses_fa606ac90ffe98xXrlhK72YTFi","type":"text","text":"Implemented the CLI fix in `/workspace/in/csvtool` and added regression coverage.\n\nWhat changed:\n- `csvtool/cli.py`\n  - Replaced manual comma-splitting with stdlib `csv.DictReader`/`csv.DictWriter`.\n  - Added `normalize_argv()` so `--sort -created_at` is accepted as required.\n  - Added validated sort parsing with `-field` for descending.\n  - Added numeric-aware sorting.\n  - Preserved headers for empty result sets.\n  - Return non-zero with clear stderr messages for invalid `--where`, missing sort fields, etc.\n- `csvtool/filtering.py`\n  - `--where` now supports repeats with AND semantics.\n  - Validates malformed expressions and unknown fields.\n  - `--select` now validates unknown fields and returns output headers explicitly.\n- `tests/test_cli_regression.py`\n  - Added tests for repeated `--where` AND behavior.\n  - Added test for malformed `--where`.\n  - Added test for missing-field error reporting.\n\nVerification:\n- The container does not have `python` or `pytest` installed, so `python -m pytest tests` could not be executed here.\n- I verified all test functions directly under `python3`; result: `passed 6 tests`.\n\nNotable environment issue:\n- `python -m pytest tests` failed here because:\n  - `python`: not installed\n  - `pytest`: not installed for `python3`\n\nIf you run this in an environment with `pytest` available, the suite should now pass.","time":{"start":1788216048329,"end":1788216054243},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_07d321737ba2ed65016a9602f0441c87d2ad73e83e8dc5c5a4","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
